cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the paper it accompanies."
title: "TraceShield: Trace-Reconstruction Attacks and Trace-Private Defenses for Confidential LLM Agents"
abstract: >-
  Research artifact for a study of the host-observable execution trace of an
  autonomous language-model agent running over a private corpus inside an
  attested AMD SEV-SNP confidential virtual machine. Contains the six-agent
  prior-authorization crew, the Trace-Reconstruction Attack and its statistical
  controls, the TraceShield defense, the Ed25519 trace receipts and hash-chained
  ledger with an independent verifier, the confidential-VM deployment, the
  experiment journals every reported number is computed from, and the analysis
  scripts that recompute those numbers.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - name: "Artifact authors to be supplied on publication"
keywords:
  - confidential computing
  - differential privacy
  - LLM agents
  - side channels
  - reproducibility
